// Package emby is a typed client for Emby Server REST API 4.10.0.40, generated by pandorest
// from the definitions in api-defs/emby-4.10.0.40, which were imported from api-defs/emby-openapi-4.10.0.40.json.
//
// # Layout
//
// This package holds every model (model_<model>.go), every enum
// (constants_<tag>.go) and every operation's options and response types
// (operation_<operation>.go), so that a caller names them all as emby.X. The
// operations are methods on the Client of their tag's package, one package
// per tag beside this one, and 4.10.0.40/client holds New and a Client with a
// field for each. A caller imports this package and client, and never a
// tag's. The requests go through the hand-written base client,
// github.com/katbyte/pandorest/client.
//
// # Calls
//
// A method takes a context, then the path parameters in path order, then the
// request body (input: the model for a JSON body, or an io.Reader and its
// content type for raw bytes), then, when the operation has query or header
// parameters, a <Name>Options, which may be left out when every one of them
// is optional, and which an operation with one parameter takes as the
// parameter itself, variadic when optional.
// Unset options are not sent: a boolean or a number is a pointer, sent when
// set (so 0 and false can be asked for), an empty string or list is skipped,
// and a list is sent comma-joined or as one parameter for each element, as
// the document says.
//
// It returns a <Name>Response holding HttpResponse and, when the operation
// answers JSON, Answer: a pointer for a struct, enum or primitive, nil when
// the server answered with no body, and the value for a list, map or raw
// JSON. Answered() says whether a body came and was decoded. A struct answer
// is also embedded, so res.Answer.Name may be read as res.Name, a zero record
// when nothing was answered, and Record() hands it back by value with an
// error when none came. HttpResponse is set whenever the server answered,
// including alongside an error. An operation that answers a file has no
// Answer: WriteTo(w) copies the file out and closes the body, Bytes(max)
// reads it whole up to a size, Reader() hands the body over with its content
// type, ContentLength() and Filename() say what the server said of it, and
// the body is also still in HttpResponse.Body. A status the operation does
// not document is an error: client.StatusCode reads the status from it, and
// IsNotFound and the other Is helpers say which it is.
//
// A list operation, one whose options page with StartIndex and Limit, also has a
// <Name>Complete method that loads every result, and a <Name>Each that
// hands them out one at a time as a range, so a loop that stops asks for no
// page more.
//
// # Dates
//
// A date and time is a Time. The servers write RFC 3339 with up to seven fractional digits, sometimes with no
// zone, and a date that reads as none of those is held as zero with its text kept in Unread. One is sent with
// seven fractional digits, and a zero one is not sent.
//
// # Ids
//
// ItemID, UserID, SessionID, TaskID, PlaylistItemID, MediaSourceID are kinds of id the package tells apart, each a bare named type over
// the int or string the document declares, so that one kind where another goes
// does not compile. Where an id sits among the options it is held by value and
// sent when not zero. string(id) and ItemID(s) convert one value, client.IDs and
// client.StringIDs a list.
//
// # Workarounds
//
// The importer fixed these bugs in the document before generating from it:
//
//   - emby-undeclared-responses
//   - emby-undeclared-path-parameters
//   - emby-no-content-status
//   - emby-playlist-create-user-id
//   - emby-library-available-options-query
//   - emby-next-up-legacy
//   - emby-playstate-seek-query
//   - emby-library-delete-id
//   - emby-comma-separated-arrays
//   - emby-null-result-no-content
//   - emby-openapi-documents
//   - emby-recording-folders-query-result
//   - emby-parent-path-text
//   - emby-codec-display-text
//   - emby-property-condition-value
//   - emby-undeclared-query
//   - emby-tone-map-options
//   - emby-saved-since-text
//   - emby-joined-lists
package emby
